208:## Evaluate: executable sealed protocol (v1)
238:- Confidence is finite in `[0.5,1)`. For sorted samples `x` of length `n`, select the largest `k >= 1` with `P(Binomial(n,0.5) < k) <= alpha/2` for equivalence or `<= alpha` for performance. Equivalence bounds are `[x[k-1],x[n-k]]`; performance uses lower bound `x[k-1]` and an unbounded upper endpoint represented by null. No admissible `k` means insufficient measurements and VOID. At 95%, one metric needs at least six independent seed pairs; performance needs at least five timing pairs. More metrics or greater confidence can require more seeds. No bootstrap randomness or asymptotic approximation is used.
